  "lines": {
    "_doc": "Every other line draws its pictures from a pool: the offer family's own sets (offers, at their weight) and the pictures named here. devices: the line's Apple models from assets/devices.json, each in every finish it has a picture of (one alone, or up to three finishes side by side); models weighs them. pictures: cut-outs in assets/cutouts, [file, weight, what it shows]. Never a picture the owner rejected (assets/approved-assets.json), a mislabelled one (verifiedBad) or one flagged as a fake render or a crop (assets/cutout-flags.json): the build drops them and says so. cars: the vehicles in assets/vehicles.json, weighted by how recent and how common they are. maxPictures and maxBytes keep what a page loads for one line small. 2026-11-18, the owner: \"we need more assets\", \"like 3-5x the pool\", \"ideally each car in different colors\", \"more standard cars\", \"unidentified cars skip we need to know what it is with confidence\", and the car lines (classic, JDM, trucks, Toyota, Honda, BMW, Mercedes / AMG, work vans, semi trucks). cap: a line's pictures (maxPictures for the rest); colours: an Apple model's finishes (3 by default); match: every approved cut-out whose id the pattern names (less exclude), at matchWeight; cars: brands, a models pattern, vintage (\"only\", \"any\", \"never\" by default), popular [[model pattern, weight]] (iSeeCars 2025: the Camry California's most popular used car, the F-150, Silverado and Ram 1500 the country's), perModel (colours of one model), perBrand (models of one make). Each pool entry is a set of its own, so the full ad can load the one a seed draws; maxBytes bounds a line read whole.",
    "maxPictures": 40,
